Subject: [PATCH] sycl: F8_E4M3 weights (DMMV, GEMM, MUL_MAT_ID, GET_ROWS, CPY)

Local gap fill. F8_E4M3 (OCP FP8, GGML_TYPE_F8_E4M3) had no SYCL support, so FP8 checkpoints ran
their matmuls on the CPU; no other GPU backend in tree has it either (Metal only copies it).

- One-token MUL_MAT: DMMV, the qk=1 kernel the F16 / BF16 weights use.
- Batches: the f16 GEMM route. Every E4M3 value is exact in f16, so widening loses nothing.
- MUL_MAT_ID: the per-expert loop, which takes the two paths above per expert.
- GET_ROWS, and CPY / DUP to and from F32, F16 and BF16 (and F8 to F8).
- The conversions are bit-exact with ggml_f8_e4m3_to_fp32 / ggml_fp32_to_f8_e4m3: saturation to
  +-448, NaN as 0x7F, round to nearest even, subnormals. The special cases test bits: icpx compiles
  ggml-sycl with its default -fp-model=fast, which may fold isnan / isinf away.

